{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561950-on-the-use-of-virtues","id":1561950,"title":"On the Use of Virtues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-19T18:45:46-07:00","id":1561950,"title":"On the Use of Virtues","content":"So I want to sidestep the more well-trodden ground of Humanity and the Paths in this and instead look at a related system that is often overlooked IMO: namely, the Virtues.<br /> <br /> These are all pretty well known I think: Consciousness, Conviction, Self-Control, Instinct, &amp; Courage with derived attributes including Humanity/Paths and Willpower.<br /> <br /> My question is how you all interpret the virtues, to what extent you use them in your games, and what changes you\u2019ve made to them if any.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll offer something I\u2019ve been spitballing recently as an example of what I mean.<br /> <br /> IMO one of the primary/essential qualities of the vampiric condition is that they are Selfish. This is something at the core of their curse and it is the fundamental cause for the (near) inevitable tendency of vampires towards isolation (the natural trajectory of tragedy). Building up a protective edifice against this acidic Selfishness at the core of their nature is where the necessity of Paths come from and is related to the efforts that go into building up sects, coteries, clans, and other vampiric communities (such organizations appeal to a vampire\u2019s rational self-interest yes but also provide concrete structures which can offer resistance to the path of least resistance for each individual - but the tragic nature of vampirism is that every such vampiric society is doomed to dissolution because of the inescapable Selfishness at the core of each member).<br /> <br /> This Selfishness (called the Beast) wants (if it\u2019s able to want anything) to dissolve all barriers to single-minded pursuit of its own interests without any concern or care for others - which inevitably becomes the inhuman revenant wights. The Paths are ideological structures built as barriers between the vampire as they exist at time of embrace and the pure expression of the Beast that is the Wight. The Paths are dependent on the Virtues for their foundation, for resisting generation, and the Will to pursue that which is contrary to the Vampire\u2019s inclination.<br /> <br /> To that end I\u2019m entertaining a modified virtue system which uses Conscience, Conviction, and Self-Control (which has Courage folded into it, I\u2019m open to alt names for this. Consciousness here represents Sympathy - it is natural and intuitive concern/pity/empathy for others, that stops you from pursuing your self-interest at other\u2019s expense. Conviction is one\u2019s ethical principles and commitment to them, whatever they might be, so long as they can be used as a reason not to pursue your Selfish interest above all else. Consciousness+Conviction form the foundation of Humanity (I haven\u2019t gotten into the details of how it might effect the Paths, the main issue being how to handle Instinct, which I\u2019m considering having as a substitution option for Self-Control still). Self-Control is the basis for your willpower score as before and is thus concerned with holding yourself back from when your desires, fears, or anger may cause you to do something your rational self doesn\u2019t want to do.<br /> <br /> Under this system, the virtues would be something that was rolled prior to sins that the Beast desires to commit (if the player is conscious; if unconscious for the crime they\u2019d be allowed to roll Consciousness or Conviction afterwards to feel guilt/shame and avoid degeneration as usual), to determine if the character can resist their desires (or if they want to), with willpower expenditure allowed. The ST should only push for sins one or two levels below the characters current level for this, to represent the grinding procession of the Beast - although players can still volunteer to commit worse sins if they so choose (with an auto degeneration - it doesn\u2019t matter if you regret it, if your virtues can\u2019t prevent you from sacrificing your higher self than they\u2019ve failed in their purpose and the Beast\u2019s final victory is closer at hand.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if this system would be better and it\u2019s still quite unpolished, but it\u2019s an example of how tweaking the virtues might serve one interpretation of the game and its themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T19:58:21-07:00","id":1561953,"title":"","content":"I think first your presentation is sound, but lacks one important consideration: vampires are also human.<br /> <br /> That's important in the game. The Beast is an unnatural force of selfishness, sure, but this is a problem not because it contends with self-interest, but because it conflicts with human needs.<br /> <br /> And yes, it includes the Sabbat. Teenager edge lords are human, ruthless mafia bosses are human, being deliberately monstrous is human to the core. And it's this low caps humanity that longs for company, society and meaning.<br /> <br /> Second let's follow proper design process. We have to understand what are the roles the Virtues have in the game, regardless of fluff:<br /> <br /> 1. Consciousness/Conviction: roll to avoid degeneration.<br /> <br /> 2. Self-Control/Instinct: roll to manage Frenzy.<br /> <br /> 3. Courage: roll to avoid R\u00f6tschreck.<br /> <br /> 4. 1 + 2 = Humanity/Path Rating.<br /> <br /> 5. 3 = Willpower.<br /> <br /> 6. There are Primary and Alternative 1 &amp; 2, that's deliberate: alternative starts 1 dot lower. That affects the impact of choosing a Path. It creates a cost to choose a Path.<br /> <br /> 7. They are always rolled alone, limiting your Pool to 1-5 dice.<br /> <br /> 8. Roll triggers don't cross boundaries: each Virtue always affect the same functions.<br /> <br /> This structure isn't sacred, but understanding it is necessary to choose between adopting it or ditching it. It takes those 3 kinds of rolls, resist Frenzy, degenerate and resist R\u00f6tschreck, set them as a module apart, untouched by other systems, limit the Pool, force choices between higher Willpower or higher Path and keep the three rolls distinct, do characters have clear strengths between those three situations.<br /> <br /> Do you want to keep this structure? That's more important now than how you define them for roleplay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}